  "label": "an upgrade reading a joined member's body equal to the item's clears the item's conflict",
  "note": "the store 187 left: b joined the card at s1 without its body, recorded as the item's conflict with no conflict_object. b's base names s1 and no body, so its upgrade fetches the body, c1, the item's own. A body read equal to the item's is no divergence, whatever the collection's policy: the item's conflict clears, and b's base takes c1 at s1 and its shared_object c1, as a binding's own conflict clears on its own body (SYNC.md §5, §6, §9). Nothing is kept: no body was lost. Under manual, landing c1 in conflict_object would leave a conflict between two equal bodies for a person to settle, on every card a second address book shares",
